      "content": "1. Himalayan Mountain Ranges"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The physical geography of India is prominently divided into Northern Himalayan Ranges and Southern Peninsular Ranges.",
        "Himalayan mountain passes serve as key strategic and trade routes across high-altitude terrain.",
        "The Peninsular Plateau is broadly divided into the Central Highlands and the Deccan Plateau.",
        "Plateau classifications in India include Intermontane (enclosed by mountains) and Piedmont (at the foot of mountains) plateaus.",
        "Understanding the highest points of major mountain ranges and plateaus is essential for spatial geographic mapping."
      ],
      "id": "12yisf2"
    },
